      ],
      "content": "1, 839                                    CASTLE Street                                        (West Side)                                        BERKHAMSTED SCHOOL CHAPEL SP 9907 NW 1/107 II                            GV 2. 1894-5 by Charles Henry Rew in Tudor style.  Red brick exterior stone dressed.  Interior: tall steep flight of steps to sanctuary reputedly inspired by the plan of Santa Maria dei Miracoli at Venice.  Vestry underneath sanctuary, shallow transepts on either side of steps.  VCH II, p 165. Berkhamsted School Old Building, School Chapel and New Hall form a group, Listing NGR: SP9942807855"
    }
